-- coa20-part27-supp.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 27 (Mergers and divisions of public companies), Chapter 4 (Supplementary provisions),
-- ss 935 to 941, lines 13035-13131 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. LAYER 1, objective. Answers are as in coa20-part27-merger.l4.


-- ===========================================================================================================
§ `Part 27, Chapter 4 -- Supplementary provisions`
-- ===========================================================================================================

§§ `Expert's report: valuation by another person (s 935)`

-- "it appears to an expert" and "it is reasonable" are the expert's own judgments: plain inputs, never guessed.
-- JURAL the expert: power to arrange for or accept another person's valuation | the other person and the merging companies: liability
-- src:13038 | (1) Where it appears to an expert—
-- src:13039 | (a) that a valuation is reasonably necessary to enable him to draw up his report, and
-- src:13040 | (b) that it is reasonable for that valuation, or part of it, to be made by (or for him to accept a valuation made by) another person who—
-- src:13041 | (i) appears to him to have the requisite knowledge and experience to make the valuation or that part of it, and
-- src:13042 | (ii) meets the independence requirement in section 936,
-- src:13043 | he may arrange for or accept such a valuation, together with a report which will enable him to make his own report under section 909 or 924.
@ref s 935(1) The expert may arrange for or accept a valuation made by another person (src:13038-13043)
GIVEN `it appears to the expert that a valuation is reasonably necessary to enable him to draw up his report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the expert that it is reasonable for that valuation, or part of it, to be made by (or for him to accept a valuation made by) another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person appears to the expert to have the requisite knowledge and experience to make the valuation or that part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 936(1) the person meets the independence requirement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 935(1) the expert may arrange for or accept the valuation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`it appears to the expert that a valuation is reasonably necessary to enable him to draw up his report`
                AND `it appears to the expert that it is reasonable for that valuation, or part of it, to be made by (or for him to accept a valuation made by) another person`
                AND `that person appears to the expert to have the requisite knowledge and experience to make the valuation or that part of it`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where it appears to an expert— (a) that a valuation is reasonably necessary ..., and (b) that it is reasonable for that valuation ... to be made by ... another person who— (i) appears to him to have the requisite knowledge and experience" (an unmet "where")
        IF `s 936(1) the person meets the independence requirement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) meets the independence requirement in section 936"
        IF `s 936(1) the person meets the independence requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the other person meets the independence requirement is not answered

-- JURAL the members: claim to an expert's report that names the valuer and describes the valuation | the expert: duty to state it
-- src:13044 | (2) Where any valuation is made by a person other than the expert himself, the latter's report must state that fact and must also—
-- src:13045 | (a) state the former's name and what knowledge and experience he has to carry out the valuation, and
-- src:13046 | (b) describe so much of the undertaking, property and liabilities as was valued by the other person, and the method used to value them, and specify the date of the valuation.
@ref s 935(2) The report must state that a valuation was made by another person, who made it, and what was valued (src:13044-13046)
GIVEN `a valuation is made by a person other than the expert himself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expert's report states that fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states the name of the other person and what knowledge and experience he has to carry out the valuation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it describes so much of the undertaking, property and liabilities as was valued by the other person, and the method used to value them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it specifies the date of the valuation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 935(2) the expert's report states what the section requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a valuation is made by a person other than the expert himself`)
    THEN `s 903(1) requirement does not apply` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any valuation is made by a person other than the expert himself"
    ELSE IF `the expert's report states that fact` AND `it states the name of the other person and what knowledge and experience he has to carry out the valuation`
            AND `it describes so much of the undertaking, property and liabilities as was valued by the other person, and the method used to value them` AND `it specifies the date of the valuation`
         THEN `s 903(1) requirement complied with`
         ELSE `s 903(1) requirement not complied with` -- a bare "must" not done (fork F3)

§§ `Experts and valuers: independence requirement (s 936)`

-- (1) "only if": a person meets the requirement only if none of the disqualifying relationships exists. The connections "specified by regulations made by the
-- Secretary of State" are not in the sources: an input (NOTHING = not known).
-- JURAL the members and creditors: claim to an independent expert | the expert and valuer: disability to act unless independent
-- src:13048 | (1) A person meets the independence requirement for the purposes of section 909 or 924 (expert's report) or section 935 (valuation by another person) only if—
-- src:13049 | (a) he is not—
-- src:13050 | (i) an officer or employee of any of the companies concerned in the scheme, or
-- src:13051 | (ii) a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner;
-- src:13052 | (b) he is not—
-- src:13053 | (i) an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of any of the companies concerned in the scheme, or
-- src:13054 | (ii) a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner; and
-- src:13055 | (c) there does not exist between—
-- src:13056 | (i) the person or an associate of his, and
-- src:13057 | (ii) any of the companies concerned in the scheme or an associated undertaking of such a company,
-- src:13058 | a connection of any such description as may be specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 936(1) A person meets the independence requirement only if he has none of the listed connections with the companies concerned (src:13048-13058)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or employee of any of the companies concerned in the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of any of the companies concerned in the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a partner or employee of an officer or employee of an associated undertaking, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there exists between the person or an associate of his and any of the companies concerned in the scheme or an associated undertaking of such a company a connection of a description specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 936(1) the person meets the independence requirement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is an officer or employee of any of the companies concerned in the scheme` OR `the person is a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person meets the independence requirement ... only if— (a) he is not— (i) an officer or employee of any of the companies concerned in the scheme, or (ii) a partner or employee of such a person"
        IF `the person is an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of any of the companies concerned in the scheme` OR `the person is a partner or employee of an officer or employee of an associated undertaking, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) he is not— (i) an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of any of the companies concerned in the scheme, or (ii) a partner or employee of such a person"
        IF `there exists between the person or an associate of his and any of the companies concerned in the scheme or an associated undertaking of such a company a connection of a description specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) there does not exist between ... a connection of any such description as may be specified by regulations"
        IF `there exists between the person or an associate of his and any of the companies concerned in the scheme or an associated undertaking of such a company a connection of a description specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the regulations specifying connections are not among the sources
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- JURAL the auditor of a company: immunity from being treated as an officer or employee for this purpose | the merging companies: no-right to treat the auditor as disqualified
-- src:13059 | (2) An auditor of a company is not regarded as an officer or employee of the company for this purpose.
@ref s 936(2) An auditor of a company is not regarded as an officer or employee of the company for this purpose (src:13059)
GIVEN `the person is an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 936(2) the person is regarded as an officer or employee of the company for the purposes of section 936` MEANS
    IF `the person is an auditor of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An auditor of a company is not regarded as an officer or employee of the company for this purpose"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) says nothing of anyone who is not an auditor

-- src:13061 | (a) the “companies concerned in the scheme” means every transferor and existing transferee company;
@ref s 936(3)(a) "the companies concerned in the scheme" (src:13061)
GIVEN `the company is a transferor company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is an existing transferee company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 936(3)(a) the company is a company concerned in the scheme` MEANS
    IF `the company is a transferor company` OR `the company is an existing transferee company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the “companies concerned in the scheme” means every transferor and existing transferee company"

-- src:13062 | (b) “associated undertaking”, in relation to a company, means—
-- src:13063 | (i) a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking of the company, or
-- src:13064 | (ii) a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking of the company; and
@ref s 936(3)(b) "associated undertaking" (src:13062-13064)
GIVEN `s 1162(2) the undertaking is a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1162(4) the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 936(3)(b) the undertaking is an associated undertaking of the company` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST TRUE) (LIST `s 1162(2) the undertaking is a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking of the company`, `s 1162(4) the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking of the company`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF elem NOTHING (LIST `s 1162(2) the undertaking is a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking of the company`, `s 1162(4) the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking of the company`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 1162 (and Schedule 7) answer parent and subsidiary undertakings outside this range
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“associated undertaking”, in relation to a company, means— (i) a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking of the company, or (ii) a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking of the company"

-- src:13065 | (c) “associate” has the meaning given by section 937.
@ref s 936(3)(c) "associate" has the meaning given by section 937 (src:13065)
GIVEN `s 937 the person is an associate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 936(3)(c) the person is an associate` MEANS
    `s 937 the person is an associate`

-- src:13066 | (4) Regulations under this section are subject to negative resolution procedure.
-- s 936(4): regulations under this section are subject to negative resolution procedure: machinery (inert, reason 2). No L4.

§§ `Experts and valuers: meaning of "associate" (s 937)`

-- JURAL none (a signpost: the section defines a term for section 936)
-- src:13068 | (1) This section defines “associate” for the purposes of section 936 (experts and valuers: independence requirement).
@ref s 937(1) This section defines "associate" for the purposes of section 936 (src:13068)
GIVEN `the purpose is that of section 936 (experts and valuers: independence requirement)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 937(1) the definition applies` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is that of section 936 (experts and valuers: independence requirement)` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "defines “associate” for the purposes of section 936"

DECLARE `s 937 kind of the person in relation to whom associate is defined` IS ONE OF
    `s 937(2) an individual`
    `s 937(3) a body corporate`
    `s 937(4) a partnership that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed`
    `s 937(5) a partnership that is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed`

DECLARE `s 937 relationship of the person to the other` IS ONE OF
    `s 937 a spouse, civil partner, minor child or step-child of the individual`
    `s 937 a body corporate of which the other is a director (for a limited liability partnership, a member)`
    `s 937 an employee of the other`
    `s 937 a partner of the other`
    `s 937 a body corporate in the same group as the other`
    `s 937 an employee or partner of a body corporate in the same group as the other`
    `s 937 a person who is an associate of a partner in the partnership`
    `s 937 any other relationship`

-- (6): in relation to a limited liability partnership, for "director" read "member": the second constructor above is read that way (fork F11).
-- JURAL none (a definition)
-- src:13069 | (2) In relation to an individual, “associate” means—
-- src:13070 | (a) that individual's spouse or civil partner or minor child or step-child,
-- src:13071 | (b) any body corporate of which that individual is a director, and
-- src:13072 | (c) any employee or partner of that individual.
-- src:13073 | (3) In relation to a body corporate, “associate” means—
-- src:13074 | (a) any body corporate of which that body is a director,
-- src:13075 | (b) any body corporate in the same group as that body, and
-- src:13076 | (c) any employee or partner of that body or of any body corporate in the same group.
-- src:13077 | (4) In relation to a partnership that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed, “associate” means—
-- src:13078 | (a) any body corporate of which that partnership is a director,
-- src:13079 | (b) any employee of or partner in that partnership, and
-- src:13080 | (c) any person who is an associate of a partner in that partnership.
-- src:13081 | (5) In relation to a partnership that is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed, “associate” means any person who is an associate of any of the partners.
-- src:13082 | (6) In this section, in relation to a limited liability partnership, for “director” read “member”.
@ref s 937(2)-(6) "associate" in relation to an individual, a body corporate and a partnership (src:13069-13082)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 937 kind of the person in relation to whom associate is defined`
      relationship IS A `s 937 relationship of the person to the other`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 937 the person is an associate` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 937(2) an individual` THEN
        CONSIDER relationship
        WHEN `s 937 a spouse, civil partner, minor child or step-child of the individual` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 937 a body corporate of which the other is a director (for a limited liability partnership, a member)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 937 an employee of the other` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 937 a partner of the other` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to an individual, “associate” means— (a) that individual's spouse or civil partner or minor child or step-child, (b) any body corporate of which that individual is a director, and (c) any employee or partner of that individual"
    WHEN `s 937(3) a body corporate` THEN
        CONSIDER relationship
        WHEN `s 937 a body corporate of which the other is a director (for a limited liability partnership, a member)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 937 a body corporate in the same group as the other` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 937 an employee of the other` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 937 a partner of the other` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 937 an employee or partner of a body corporate in the same group as the other` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a body corporate, “associate” means— (a) any body corporate of which that body is a director, (b) any body corporate in the same group as that body, and (c) any employee or partner of that body or of any body corporate in the same group"
    WHEN `s 937(4) a partnership that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed` THEN
        CONSIDER relationship
        WHEN `s 937 a body corporate of which the other is a director (for a limited liability partnership, a member)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 937 an employee of the other` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 937 a partner of the other` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 937 a person who is an associate of a partner in the partnership` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a partnership that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed, “associate” means— (a) any body corporate of which that partnership is a director, (b) any employee of or partner in that partnership, and (c) any person who is an associate of a partner in that partnership"
    WHEN `s 937(5) a partnership that is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed` THEN
        CONSIDER relationship
        WHEN `s 937 a person who is an associate of a partner in the partnership` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a partnership that is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed, “associate” means any person who is an associate of any of the partners"

§§ `Power of court to summon meeting of members or creditors of existing transferee company (s 938)`

-- JURAL the members or creditors of the existing transferee company: liability to be summoned | the court: power
-- src:13085 | (1) The court may order a meeting of—
-- src:13086 | (a) the members of an existing transferee company, or any class of them, or
-- src:13087 | (b) the creditors of an existing transferee company, or any class of them,
-- src:13088 | to be summoned in such manner as the court directs.
@ref s 938(1) The court may order a meeting of the members or creditors of an existing transferee company (src:13085-13088)
GIVEN `the company is an existing transferee company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 938(1) the court may order a meeting of the members or creditors of the company` MEANS
    IF `the company is an existing transferee company` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may order a meeting of— (a) the members of an existing transferee company, ..., or (b) the creditors of an existing transferee company"

-- JURAL the company, a member or creditor: power to apply | the court: liability to hear it
-- src:13089 | (2) An application for such an order may be made by—
-- src:13090 | (a) the company concerned,
-- src:13091 | (b) a member or creditor of the company, or
-- src:13092 | (c) if the company is being wound up, the liquidator, or
-- src:13093 | (d) if the company is in administration, the administrator.
@ref s 938(2) Who may apply (src:13089-13093)
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 896(2) applicant`
      `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is in administration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 938(2) the person may apply to the court` MEANS
    CONSIDER applicant
    WHEN `s 896(2) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 896(2) a creditor of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 896(2) a member of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 896(2) the liquidator of the company` THEN
        IF `the company is being wound up` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the company is being wound up, the liquidator" (an unmet "if" on a power the text gives: fork F33)
    WHEN `s 896(2) the administrator of the company` THEN
        IF `the company is in administration` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the company is in administration, the administrator" (an unmet "if" on a power the text gives: fork F33)
    WHEN `s 896(2) any other person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the list of those who may apply does not say "only"

-- src:13094 | (3) Section 323 (representation of corporations at meetings) applies to a meeting of creditors under this section as to a meeting of the company (references to a member being read as references to a creditor).
@ref s 938(3) Section 323 applies to a meeting of creditors under this section (src:13094)
GIVEN `the meeting is a meeting of creditors under section 938` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 938(3) section 323 applies to the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is a meeting of creditors under section 938` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies to a meeting of creditors under this section"

§§ `Court to fix date for transfer of undertaking etc of transferor company (s 939)`

-- JURAL the members and creditors, the transferor and the transferee companies: claim that the court fix the date | the court: duty to fix it
-- src:13096 | (1) Where the court sanctions the compromise or arrangement, it must—
-- src:13097 | (a) in the order sanctioning the compromise or arrangement, or
-- src:13098 | (b) in a subsequent order under section 900 or, as the case may be, section 901J (powers of court to facilitate reconstruction or amalgamation),
-- src:13099 | fix a date on which the transfer (or transfers) to the transferee company (or transferee companies) of the undertaking, property and liabilities of the transferor company is (or are) to take place.
@ref s 939(1) Where the court sanctions the compromise or arrangement, it must fix a date for the transfer (src:13096-13099)
GIVEN `the court sanctions the compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has fixed a date for the transfer (or transfers), in the order sanctioning the compromise or arrangement or in a subsequent order under section 900 or section 901J` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 939(1) the court has fixed a date for the transfer` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the court sanctions the compromise or arrangement`)
    THEN `s 903(1) requirement does not apply` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court sanctions the compromise or arrangement"
    ELSE IF `the court has fixed a date for the transfer (or transfers), in the order sanctioning the compromise or arrangement or in a subsequent order under section 900 or section 901J`
         THEN `s 903(1) requirement complied with`
         ELSE `s 903(1) requirement not complied with` -- a bare "must" not done (fork F3)

-- src:13100 | (2) Any such order that provides for the dissolution of the transferor company must fix the same date for the dissolution.
@ref s 939(2) An order providing for dissolution of the transferor company must fix the same date for the dissolution (src:13100)
GIVEN `the order provides for the dissolution of the transferor company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order fixes the same date for the dissolution as for the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 939(2) the order fixes the same date for the dissolution` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the order provides for the dissolution of the transferor company`)
    THEN `s 903(1) requirement does not apply` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any such order that provides for the dissolution of the transferor company"
    ELSE IF `the order fixes the same date for the dissolution as for the transfer`
         THEN `s 903(1) requirement complied with`
         ELSE `s 903(1) requirement not complied with` -- a bare "must" not done (fork F3)

-- "not later than six months after the date fixed under subsection (1)": the sixth calendar month after the date is the last day (the library's `add months`).
-- JURAL the transferor company: duty to take the steps by the date | the court: duty to fix the date; the transferee companies and members: claim to the transfer
-- src:13101 | (3) If it is necessary for the transferor company to take steps to ensure that the undertaking, property and liabilities are fully transferred, the court must fix a date, not later than six months after the date fixed under subsection (1), by which such steps must be taken.
@ref s 939(3) If steps are needed to ensure the transfer, the court must fix a date, not later than six months after the transfer date, by which they must be taken (src:13101)
GIVEN `it is necessary for the transferor company to take steps to ensure that the undertaking, property and liabilities are fully transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date fixed under subsection (1) for the transfer` IS A DATE
      `date fixed by the court by which the steps must be taken` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 939(3) the court has fixed a date for the steps within six months` MEANS
    IF NOT (`it is necessary for the transferor company to take steps to ensure that the undertaking, property and liabilities are fully transferred`)
    THEN `s 903(1) requirement does not apply` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If it is necessary for the transferor company to take steps to ensure that the undertaking, property and liabilities are fully transferred"
    ELSE IF `date fixed by the court by which the steps must be taken` AT MOST (`add months` `date fixed under subsection (1) for the transfer` 6)
         THEN `s 903(1) requirement complied with`
         ELSE `s 903(1) requirement not complied with` -- "not later than six months after the date fixed under subsection (1)" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

-- src:13102 | (4) In that case, the court may postpone the dissolution of the transferor company until that date.
@ref s 939(4) In that case the court may postpone the dissolution of the transferor company until that date (src:13102)
GIVEN `a date has been fixed under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 939(4) the court may postpone the dissolution of the transferor company until that date` MEANS
    IF `a date has been fixed under subsection (3)` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In that case, the court may postpone the dissolution"

-- src:13103 | (5) The court may postpone or further postpone the date fixed under subsection (3) if it is satisfied that the steps mentioned cannot be completed by the date (or latest date) fixed under that subsection.
@ref s 939(5) The court may postpone or further postpone the date if it is satisfied that the steps cannot be completed by then (src:13103)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the steps mentioned cannot be completed by the date (or latest date) fixed under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 939(5) the court may postpone or further postpone the date` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the steps mentioned cannot be completed by the date (or latest date) fixed under subsection (3)` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it is satisfied that the steps mentioned cannot be completed by the date (or latest date) fixed under that subsection"

§§ `Liability of transferee companies for each other's defaults (s 940)`

DECLARE `s 940(2) Part under which the compromise or arrangement is sanctioned` IS ONE OF
    `s 940(2) Part 26`
    `s 940(2A) Part 26A`

-- (2) Part 26: a majority in number representing 75% in value of the creditors (or a class) present and voting agree; (2A) Part 26A: a number representing 75% in value.
-- JURAL the creditors who so agree: no claim against the other transferee companies | the creditors: disability; the transferee companies: immunity
-- src:13108 | (2) If, in the case of a compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26, a majority in number representing 75% in value of the creditors or any class of creditors of the transferor company, present and voting either in person or by proxy at a meeting summoned for the purposes of agreeing to the scheme, so agree, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to the liabilities owed to the creditors or that class of creditors.
-- src:13109 | (2A) If, in the case of a compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26A, a number representing 75% in value of the creditors or any class of creditors of the transferor company, present and voting either in person or by proxy at a meeting summoned for the purposes of agreeing to the scheme, so agree, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to the liabilities owed to the creditors or that class of creditors.
@ref s 940(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to creditors who agree by the majority the section names (src:13108-13109)
GIVEN part IS A `s 940(2) Part under which the compromise or arrangement is sanctioned`
      `the number of the creditors of the transferor company (or of the class) present and voting at a meeting summoned for the purposes of agreeing to the scheme` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of them who agree` IS A NUMBER
      `the value represented by those present and voting` IS A NUMBER
      `the value represented by those who agree` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 940(2) subsection (1) does not apply in relation to the liabilities owed to those creditors` MEANS
    CONSIDER part
    WHEN `s 940(2) Part 26` THEN
        IF 2 TIMES `the number of them who agree` GREATER THAN `the number of the creditors of the transferor company (or of the class) present and voting at a meeting summoned for the purposes of agreeing to the scheme`
           AND `the value represented by those who agree` AT LEAST (0.75 TIMES `the value represented by those present and voting`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, in the case of a compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26, a majority in number representing 75% in value of the creditors ..., so agree, subsection (1) does not apply" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
    WHEN `s 940(2A) Part 26A` THEN
        IF `the value represented by those who agree` AT LEAST (0.75 TIMES `the value represented by those present and voting`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, in the case of a compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26A, a number representing 75% in value of the creditors ... so agree, subsection (1) does not apply" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))

-- (3): not liable for an amount greater than the net value transferred: the value at the time of the transfer of the property transferred to it less the liabilities
-- transferred at that date. A negative net value is read as nil (fork F12).
-- src:13110 | (3) A transferee company is not liable under this section for an amount greater than the net value transferred to it under the scheme.
-- src:13111 | The “net value transferred” is the value at the time of the transfer of the property transferred to it under the scheme less the amount at that date of the liabilities so transferred.
@ref s 940(3) A transferee company is not liable for an amount greater than the net value transferred to it (src:13110-13111)
GIVEN `the value at the time of the transfer of the property transferred to the company under the scheme` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount at that date of the liabilities so transferred` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 940(3) the net value transferred` MEANS
    IF `the value at the time of the transfer of the property transferred to the company under the scheme` MINUS `the amount at that date of the liabilities so transferred` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the value at the time of the transfer of the property transferred to the company under the scheme` MINUS `the amount at that date of the liabilities so transferred`
    ELSE 0

-- (1): each transferee company is jointly and severally liable for any liability transferred to any other transferee company, to the extent that other company has made default.
-- The answer is the amount (pounds) for which the company is liable: nothing where (2) or (2A) excludes the liability; at most the net value transferred (3).
-- JURAL the creditor: claim against each transferee company, jointly and severally | each transferee company: liability for the others' defaults
-- src:13106 | (1) In the case of a division, each transferee company is jointly and severally liable for any liability transferred to any other transferee company under the scheme to the extent that the other company has made default in satisfying that liability.
-- src:13107 | This is subject to the following provisions.
@ref s 940(1) In a division each transferee company is jointly and severally liable for a liability transferred to another transferee company to the extent of that company's default (src:13106-13107)
GIVEN `the scheme is a division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability was transferred to another transferee company under the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 940(2) subsection (1) does not apply in relation to the liabilities owed to those creditors` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the liability to the extent that the other company has made default in satisfying it` IS A NUMBER
      `s 940(3) the net value transferred` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 940(1) the amount for which the transferee company is liable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the scheme is a division` AND `the liability was transferred to another transferee company under the scheme`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a division, each transferee company is jointly and severally liable for any liability transferred to any other transferee company under the scheme"
        IF `s 940(2) subsection (1) does not apply in relation to the liabilities owed to those creditors` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST 0 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (1) does not apply in relation to the liabilities owed to the creditors or that class of creditors"
        IF `s 940(2) subsection (1) does not apply in relation to the liabilities owed to those creditors` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the creditors agreed by the majority is not known
        IF `the amount of the liability to the extent that the other company has made default in satisfying it` GREATER THAN `s 940(3) the net value transferred`
            THEN JUST `s 940(3) the net value transferred` -- "not liable ... for an amount greater than the net value transferred to it"
        OTHERWISE JUST `the amount of the liability to the extent that the other company has made default in satisfying it`

§§ `Disregard of website failures beyond control of company (s 940A)`

DECLARE `s 940A(2) provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 940A(2)(a) section 906A(6)`
    `s 940A(2)(b) section 911A(4)`
    `s 940A(2)(c) section 916(3B) and (4B)`
    `s 940A(2)(d) section 917(3B) and (4B)`
    `s 940A(2)(e) section 918(2B) and (3B)`
    `s 940A(2)(f) section 921A(6)`
    `s 940A(2)(g) section 926A(4)`
    `s 940A(2)(h) section 931(3B) and (4B)`
    `s 940A(2)(i) section 932(2B) and (3B)`
    `s 940A(2) any other provision`

-- src:13117 | (2) The provisions referred to above are—
-- src:13118 | (a) section 906A(6),
-- src:13119 | (b) section 911A(4),
-- src:13120 | (c) section 916(3B) and (4B),
-- src:13121 | (d) section 917(3B) and (4B),
-- src:13122 | (e) section 918(2B) and (3B),
-- src:13123 | (f) section 921A(6),
-- src:13124 | (g) section 926A(4),
-- src:13125 | (h) section 931(3B) and (4B), and
-- src:13126 | (i) section 932(2B) and (3B).
@ref s 940A(2) The provisions referred to in subsection (1) (src:13117-13126)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 940A(2) provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 940A(2) the provision is one of those to which section 940A(1) applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `s 940A(2) any other provision` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provisions referred to above are" (a defining list, read as closed: fork F13)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13114 | (1) A failure to make information or a document available on the website throughout a period specified in any of the provisions mentioned in subsection (2) is to be disregarded if—
-- src:13115 | (a) it is made available on the website for part of that period, and
-- src:13116 | (b) the failure to make it available throughout that period is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid.
@ref s 940A(1) A failure to make information or a document available on the website throughout a period is disregarded if it was available for part of the period and the failure is wholly attributable to circumstances beyond the company's control (src:13114-13116)
GIVEN `s 940A(2) the provision is one of those to which section 940A(1) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the information or document is made available on the website for part of that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure to make it available throughout that period is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 940A(1) the failure is to be disregarded` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 940A(2) the provision is one of those to which section 940A(1) applies` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the provision is one of those listed is not known
        IF NOT (`s 940A(2) the provision is one of those to which section 940A(1) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                AND `the information or document is made available on the website for part of that period`
                AND `the failure to make it available throughout that period is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be disregarded if— (a) it is made available on the website for part of that period, and (b) the failure to make it available throughout that period is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Meaning of "liabilities" and "property" (s 941)`

-- src:13129 | In this Part—
-- src:13130 | “liabilities” includes duties;
@ref s 941 "liabilities" includes duties (src:13129-13130)
GIVEN `the thing is a duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 941 the thing is a liability` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a duty` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“liabilities” includes duties"

-- src:13131 | “property” includes property, rights and powers of every description.
@ref s 941 "property" includes property, rights and powers of every description (src:13131)
GIVEN `the thing is property, a right or a power of any description` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 941 the thing is property` MEANS
    IF `the thing is property, a right or a power of any description` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“property” includes property, rights and powers of every description"

